From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:41:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wallpapers/image: Read a transient image again for a new
 window

TransientImage drops its image once it is a texture, and the texture
belongs to the window it was made for: releaseResources() hands it to
that window's render thread when the item leaves the window. Moved into
another window, the item found its options unchanged, said Ready and
drew nothing there, as no image was left to make a texture from. The
lock screen's wallpaper showed only its background colour whenever the
greeter moved it into a window of its own after the image had loaded,
and an image wallpaper moved between screens' windows would do the same.

When the texture is released, forget the options it was made with, so
that the next window the item renders to reads the image again.

Test: testtransientimage, an image moved from one window to another
shows in the second (red before, green after).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
